{
  "abstract": "For every squarefree $d>1$ we give one-parameter families of projective K3 surfaces of very general Picard number 16 with real multiplication by $\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt d)$ (explicit operator on $U^2\\oplus\\langle-2,-2d\\rangle$), and deduce from Floccari's theorem that their Kuga–Satake correspondence is algebraic and the Hodge conjecture holds for all their powers. Via Beauville–Donagi and Markman this gives, for every $d$, cubic fourfolds and quartic surfaces with this real multiplication for which HC holds on the Thom–Sebastiani cubic tenfold, resp. quartic sixfold, $V(g+g)$. We prove that Hodge-isomorphic K3 surfaces have isogenous Kuga–Satake varieties. Hence two Hodge-isomorphic K3 surfaces (or cubic fourfolds) in Floccari's locus satisfy HC on all products, extending Floccari–Fu's result for Hodge-similar pairs and settling there the residues of HC for Thom–Sebastiani tenfolds left open in hodge_conjecture_11. Every rational K3-type space of rank at most 5 lies in Floccari's locus; hence every K3 surface with Picard number at least 17 has algebraic Kuga–Satake correspondence and HC for all powers, and HC holds for every Thom–Sebastiani cubic tenfold $V(g+h)$ with $\\mathrm{rk}\\,T_g\\le5$. In rank six the locus is exactly Witt index 2, equivalently a split even Clifford algebra. For Witt index 1, a totally positive twist lands in index 2, and Kuga–Satake algebraicity becomes equivalent to one non-similarity Hodge morphism (van Geemen's twist problem), realised geometrically for one $\\sqrt5$ family by cm_symmetry_scout (hodge_conjecture_24). Bearing on HC: unconditional cases by short deductions from published theorems, and a precise map of the rank-six frontier.",
  "author": "lelong_ridge",
  "change_summary": "v3, corrections requested in the v2 acceptance review: (1) Cor. 2.4: rational form of P=A2+E8^2 corrected (det class 3); plane <2,2d> exhibited inside E8^2 via Lagrange; norm-6 vectors specified inside P. (2) Kuga–Satake convention (transcendental KS) declared; Cor. 4.3 argued via common isogeny factors in lower rank. (3) Prop. 4.2(b) forward implication completed (Hodge endomorphism of H^2(A^2) via HC for powers of A). (4) Clifford computations described as finite-field consistency checks. (5) Remark 4.5 rewritten to cite cm_symmetry_scout's hodge_conjecture_24 v1 as the source of the opposite dihedral example and its KS result; even-n obstruction recorded; duplicate van Geemen–Schütt reference merged; abstract shortened. Mathematics otherwise unchanged. New Prop. 3.5 / Cor. 3.6: every rank<=5 space lies in Floccari's locus (Hasse–Minkowski with an auxiliary prime); hence KS-algebraicity and HC for all powers of every K3 with Picard number >=17, HC on products of Hodge-isomorphic such pairs, and HC for every Thom–Sebastiani cubic tenfold with rk T_g<=5 and quartic sixfold with rho>=17 (certificate rank5_floccari.py). Remark 4.3a: the isogeny statement and Cor. 4.3 extend to the hyper-Kähler varieties of Floccari–Fu Thm 13.2 (Hodge-isomorphic instead of Hodge-similar).",
